DIAGNOSTIQUE - STABLE(ish)
==========================

How to use
----------

Recommended - download the latest stable 1.23 version. This is compiled into a Windows binary so you don't need any of the dependencies, or to have Python installed.


Databases
---------
You'll need to download the databases (80-100mb zip) separately and copy to the db folder
- STABLE - July 21: https://bitbucket.org/thoste5/diagnostique/downloads/db.zip
- EXPERIMENTAL - July 22:  https://bitbucket.org/thoste5/diagnostique/downloads/db-jul-22.zip


For the EvolutionXS to work properly
------------------------------------

**IMPORTANT** - You MUST run Diagnostique from the same disk drive that the following folders are installed on (the C drive). Otherwise, you will encounter strange errors and the VCI will not work. See documentation for more information about this.

If you are using with the EvolutionXS VCI (Windows only) - currently the only supported adapter, you need to have the drivers and necessary files installed already (a working diagbox install) or:

- The actual hardware drivers installer
- The /AWRoot/drv folder
- The /AWRoot/dtrd/comm/data folder and contents (no need for the FDB databases)

The comm/data folder contains some file that is hardcode referenced from the actia VCI DLL (no kidding) and it won't work without it


Dependencies
------------
You must use 32BIT python or the VCI DLL will not work. If you're not using the VCI, use what you like :)

> pip3 install kivy kivy-garden pyserial pyyaml

Then you need the following kivy garden flower

> garden install navigationdrawer

Tkinter is needed for the Treeview database browsing app

To use SocketCAN under linux you'll need

> pip3 install python-can

And to use the ELM327 bluetooth driver you'll need this. On linux you'll need libbluetooth-dev for this to work

> pip3 install pybluez

Running the main app
--------------------
From the root directory run

> python3 main.py


Running the treeview database explorer
From the treeview directory

> python main.py



